###############################################
# How It Works:
###############################################

# 1. Both workers start transactions at ~same time
# 2. Both check: task has 0 assignments ✓
# 3. First worker creates assignment → commits ✓
# 4. Second worker re-checks (OPTIMISTIC LOCK)
#    → Now sees 1 assignment
#    → Throws DOUBLE_ACCEPTANCE error
#    → Rollback transaction
# 5. Result: Only 1 assignment created!

###############################################
# Key Points:
###############################################

# ✅ Atomicity: Transaction ensures all-or-nothing
# ✅ Isolation: Serializable transactions prevent races
# ✅ Consistency: Always correct assignment count
# ✅ Durability: Committed data is permanent

# 🔒 Optimistic Lock = First Wins!

